WEBVTT

00:11.386 --> 00:13.555
- [somber music playing]
- [Moon Baek groans]

00:16.599 --> 00:17.600
How are you feeling?

00:18.184 --> 00:19.310
Hmm?

00:19.394 --> 00:22.063
Oh, yeah. Uh, not bad. Considering…

00:24.524 --> 00:25.734
I wanted to ask,

00:26.901 --> 00:28.403
what happened when you were young?

00:29.738 --> 00:30.613
Hmm?

00:33.074 --> 00:34.576
You said your mom passed away.

00:34.659 --> 00:36.661
[somber music continues]

00:39.622 --> 00:40.707
[sighs]

00:41.291 --> 00:42.876
Someone broke into our house.

00:45.587 --> 00:49.257
Everyone in my family died.
I was the only survivor.

00:51.885 --> 00:53.803
If my brother were still alive…

00:58.224 --> 01:00.060
he'd be about your age by now.

01:05.940 --> 01:07.650
You ever consider getting revenge?

01:11.237 --> 01:13.490
I mean,
you could've if you really wanted to.

01:14.074 --> 01:16.326
You could've found the guy,
hunted him down, and bang!

01:17.243 --> 01:18.495
Shot him where he stands.

01:19.245 --> 01:20.163
Not worth it.

01:20.246 --> 01:21.247
[sighs]

01:24.084 --> 01:26.753
What are you trying to say?
That you're better than all that?

01:26.836 --> 01:27.837
Above us all?

01:28.338 --> 01:30.632
Him being brought to justice
by the legal system

01:30.715 --> 01:33.134
was enough for you?
That's why you became a cop?

01:34.052 --> 01:36.262
[somber music continues]

01:36.346 --> 01:38.932
People like that don't change.
It's not that simple.

01:40.600 --> 01:44.771
The bastards who stole away my childhood
would've done it regardless.

01:45.271 --> 01:47.398
If it wasn't me,
it would've been some other poor kid.

01:47.482 --> 01:49.692
Revenge isn't always the right choice.

01:51.653 --> 01:54.155
Especially if it destroys you. [sighs]

02:01.287 --> 02:02.163
[gun clicks]

02:02.247 --> 02:04.958
[gunshot echoing]

02:05.041 --> 02:07.043
[music fades]

02:11.714 --> 02:12.924
[sighs]

02:13.925 --> 02:15.343
It all happened so fast.

02:16.344 --> 02:18.638
I still can't believe it's real.
[sniffles]

02:33.862 --> 02:35.864
[somber music playing]

02:43.288 --> 02:44.747
[sighs]

02:47.959 --> 02:49.961
[music turns uneasy]

02:52.255 --> 02:53.715
Jake just reached out to us.

02:54.591 --> 02:55.758
Why?

02:55.842 --> 02:58.720
There are a few parties interested
in what's happening in Korea.

02:58.803 --> 03:00.513
They'd like to get in touch with us.

03:02.098 --> 03:04.601
Tell him I'll decide
after meeting them personally.

03:04.684 --> 03:06.853
Good, sir. He was quite worried.

03:07.729 --> 03:08.688
About what?

03:09.189 --> 03:10.815
Me or the business?

03:12.275 --> 03:13.443
[phone buzzes]

03:18.531 --> 03:20.533
[uneasy music continues]

03:22.327 --> 03:23.453
REPORTER WANG DAE-HYEON

03:23.536 --> 03:25.496
I THINK THERE'S SOMETHING YOU SHOULD KNOW

03:25.580 --> 03:26.497
LEE DO IS AWAKE

03:29.375 --> 03:31.377
[music fades]

03:34.672 --> 03:36.007
[Do] Thank you for coming.

03:38.718 --> 03:39.886
[man 1] Years ago,

03:40.678 --> 03:44.557
when Do and I were on a mission
in a region of the Middle East…

03:45.975 --> 03:46.935
[sighs]

03:47.518 --> 03:50.313
…we saw both adults
and children holding guns,

03:50.396 --> 03:52.690
weapons piled on top of each other,
and I wondered,

03:52.774 --> 03:56.152
"What would happen if that kind of thing
happened here, in Korea?"

03:56.236 --> 03:59.447
[chuckles softly] Back then,
I couldn't even have imagined it.

03:59.530 --> 04:01.324
Not for a second. And now…

04:02.909 --> 04:05.828
So? How's the gun retrieval coming along?

04:06.412 --> 04:09.832
Well, we pivoted the investigation
in a new way after the first few killings.

04:10.333 --> 04:13.294
We realized that now
they were using real courier services.

04:13.378 --> 04:15.922
They had an innate understanding
of the nature of the Korean people

04:16.005 --> 04:18.341
and its infrastructure.
We estimate, in the past few days,

04:18.424 --> 04:20.927
that about 10,000 guns
have been distributed to the public.

04:21.010 --> 04:22.887
It was probably instigated

04:22.971 --> 04:26.808
after the footage of you getting shot
was aired on social media.

04:26.891 --> 04:29.602
[man 1] That probably managed to enhance
people's fear.

04:30.228 --> 04:33.273
If you don't wanna end up shot,
you need to protect yourself.

04:34.732 --> 04:36.109
That's what guns do.

04:37.026 --> 04:38.653
False sense of security.

04:38.736 --> 04:39.862
That's right.

04:40.613 --> 04:42.782
They truly believe
no one else can protect them,

04:42.865 --> 04:44.492
so they need to do it for themselves.

04:44.575 --> 04:46.828
And for that,
they need a gun in their hand.

04:46.911 --> 04:48.913
[brooding music playing]

04:52.709 --> 04:55.420
Uh, Manager, there's something important
for you to look at.

04:55.503 --> 04:57.088
[keys tapping]

04:57.171 --> 04:59.299
A GATHERING OF SUPPORTERS
OF GUN OWNERSHIP LEGALIZATION

04:59.382 --> 05:01.551
This began circulating on social media
a while ago.

05:01.634 --> 05:03.928
It's been shared over 300,000 times, sir.

05:04.012 --> 05:05.013
[phone buzzing]

05:08.016 --> 05:08.850
Yes, Director?

05:08.933 --> 05:10.601
The president's ready
to address the nation.

05:10.685 --> 05:12.145
If he decides to declare martial law.

05:12.228 --> 05:15.231
Korea will once again become
a country ruled by guns.

05:16.482 --> 05:17.483
Okay, listen close.

05:18.109 --> 05:20.945
We need all of you working on this.
It's top-tier priority.

05:21.029 --> 05:23.656
We need to find out
who's organizing this rally.

05:23.740 --> 05:26.367
If it becomes too large-scale,
all hell could break loose.

05:26.451 --> 05:27.785
[all] Understood, sir.

05:29.954 --> 05:31.122
[phone buzzes]

05:34.292 --> 05:35.501
Huh.

05:36.711 --> 05:37.712
What's wrong? What is it?

05:39.088 --> 05:40.173
[man 2] Look at this.

05:41.257 --> 05:42.383
What the hell?

05:43.676 --> 05:44.719
[man 1 scoffs]

05:45.219 --> 05:46.888
A pro-gun ownership rally?

05:49.390 --> 05:52.769
A gathering like this will only lead
to more people getting hurt.

05:55.021 --> 05:56.731
[crowd chanting indistinctly]

05:56.814 --> 05:58.733
The unprecedented occurrence
of mass shootings

05:58.816 --> 06:01.486
and the widespread distribution of guns
from unknown parties

06:01.569 --> 06:04.906
has led to calls for Korea
to legalize gun ownership.

06:05.615 --> 06:07.825
And pro-gun protesters
have organized themselves

06:07.909 --> 06:09.994
to make their voices heard
by the government today.

06:10.661 --> 06:13.915
In response, anti-gun protesters
have organized a counter rally,

06:13.998 --> 06:17.335
leading to concerns that a major clash
may break out between the two groups.

06:17.418 --> 06:19.670
Have any of you actually been shot?

06:19.754 --> 06:23.925
I was shot and nearly fucking died.
I was lucky to keep my arm!

06:24.008 --> 06:26.219
We've been living our lives
just fine without guns!

06:26.302 --> 06:28.137
You actually believe having no guns

06:28.221 --> 06:30.139
will keep you safer
than you were before, huh?!

06:30.223 --> 06:33.935
Our future's at stake!
We need to keep our families safe!

06:34.018 --> 06:35.978
We don't want guns in our lives ever!

06:36.062 --> 06:38.189
- Legalize guns!
- [chanting] Never! Never!

06:38.272 --> 06:42.151
- [chanting] Legalize! Legalize! Legalize!
- [chanting] Never! Never! Never!

06:45.196 --> 06:47.198
[phone buzzing]

06:51.494 --> 06:52.829
Hi, Mom.

06:52.912 --> 06:55.123
Hey, honey. Are you still working?

06:55.206 --> 06:58.668
Mm-hmm.
I'm working night shifts again this week.

06:58.751 --> 07:00.795
Oh. And you're doing okay?

07:00.878 --> 07:03.131
Of course. Why wouldn't I be okay?

07:03.214 --> 07:05.967
I heard on the news
about a lot of people getting shot lately.

07:06.050 --> 07:08.219
It must be quite chaotic
at your hospital right now.

07:08.302 --> 07:10.930
Mom, I have to get back to work.
Can I call you later?

07:11.013 --> 07:12.390
[sighs] Okay.

07:39.876 --> 07:41.085
[Do] Officer Jang,

07:41.961 --> 07:43.671
I need to get to that rally.

07:47.258 --> 07:48.259
I promise you,

07:49.469 --> 07:51.804
the sergeant will get
a proper send-off today.

07:54.557 --> 07:55.850
Thank you, Officer.

08:09.697 --> 08:11.115
- [groans]
- [nurse 1] Bitch!

08:11.616 --> 08:14.619
What did I say would happen
if you started demanding things again?

08:14.702 --> 08:16.787
- I'm sorry, miss.
- [groans in frustration]

08:17.622 --> 08:19.624
Do you really think
you've been here long enough

08:19.707 --> 08:23.377
to demand schedule changes?
Just take the shifts they give you.

08:23.461 --> 08:24.587
It won't happen again.

08:24.670 --> 08:25.588
[nurse 2 scoffs]

08:31.344 --> 08:32.178
Listen.

08:32.929 --> 08:36.682
One word to the head nurse
and your career is over.

08:36.766 --> 08:40.686
Get that through your thick skull
before you try that shit again.

08:45.399 --> 08:46.984
If she tries it again, just tell me.

08:47.068 --> 08:50.404
- [nurse 1] She's so fucking annoying.
- [nurse 2] Today's snack is dakbal.

08:50.488 --> 08:52.114
[nurse 1] From the same place
as last time?

08:52.198 --> 08:54.575
[nurse 1] Yes, of course.
There's no need to go anywhere else.

08:54.659 --> 08:56.827
[melancholic music playing]

09:17.139 --> 09:18.391
[gun clicking]

09:21.269 --> 09:22.645
[gun clatters]

09:24.730 --> 09:26.732
[tense music playing]

09:35.032 --> 09:38.828
If owning a gun becomes legalized,
we will live in a world

09:38.911 --> 09:41.205
where bulletproof vests
become a necessity,

09:41.289 --> 09:44.125
just as masks were a necessity
during the pandemic!

09:44.208 --> 09:46.460
We now need guns more than ever!

09:46.544 --> 09:49.714
[chanting] Legalize! Legalize! Legalize!

09:49.797 --> 09:52.091
Is this the kind of world
you want to be a part of?

09:52.174 --> 09:54.260
[chanting] No guns! No guns!

09:54.343 --> 09:57.430
[woman 1] The number of protesters
in favor of legalizing gun ownership

09:57.513 --> 10:00.808
has surpassed police estimates of 10,000
and is continuing to grow.

10:00.891 --> 10:03.185
[man 1] As the police prepare
for all contingencies,

10:03.269 --> 10:06.480
they are also dedicating efforts
to pursuing those responsible for…

10:06.564 --> 10:08.608
[woman 2] …out of concern
for a possible clash

10:08.691 --> 10:10.651
and the safety of the people concerned.

10:10.735 --> 10:13.571
[man 2] Blue Brown is behind the protest,
organized through social media.

10:13.654 --> 10:16.782
[woman 3] They are currently looking for
the group's base of operations,

10:16.866 --> 10:18.868
but have no leads at this time.

10:18.951 --> 10:20.745
- [phone buzzing]
- [protesters clamoring]

10:23.831 --> 10:25.833
[tense music continues]

10:26.500 --> 10:28.628
NO CALLER ID

10:39.722 --> 10:41.724
[music subsides]

10:42.725 --> 10:44.727
[footsteps echoing]

10:45.519 --> 10:47.521
[uneasy music playing]

11:10.711 --> 11:11.796
[gun clicks]

11:29.563 --> 11:31.315
You enjoy your tour in the Middle East?

11:35.444 --> 11:36.654
That's why I was chosen?

11:37.571 --> 11:38.698
[scoffs]

11:41.158 --> 11:42.284
At the beginning,

11:43.494 --> 11:44.328
it was all

11:45.955 --> 11:46.997
out of curiosity.

11:47.081 --> 11:51.293
I had such high expectations
of that guy at the gosiwon.

11:51.794 --> 11:53.587
Even though the rules aren't mandatory,

11:53.671 --> 11:56.590
the rules were still made for everyone
to follow. So I thought--

11:56.674 --> 11:59.635
Oh yeah? Why the hell do you care, huh?

11:59.719 --> 12:02.263
I'm fine, really.
I don't wanna cause any trouble.

12:02.346 --> 12:04.348
[breathing shakily]

12:05.057 --> 12:07.059
[dramatic music sting]

12:08.185 --> 12:11.355
But then I heard a police officer
swooped in from the shadows.

12:12.398 --> 12:14.150
Like a superhero on steroids.

12:15.151 --> 12:17.945
So I did some digging on that officer…

12:18.028 --> 12:18.863
TOP SECRET

12:18.946 --> 12:21.490
…and learned he was a person
who knew his way around guns

12:21.574 --> 12:22.533
and how to shoot.

12:23.492 --> 12:26.036
I found out
that now he refused to pick up a gun.

12:26.662 --> 12:27.496
That was ironic.

12:29.498 --> 12:32.001
Tell me. Was that all a facade?

12:33.335 --> 12:34.503
How real was that?

12:36.088 --> 12:38.174
And that's when I felt I truly knew you.

12:38.257 --> 12:39.633
[music fades]

12:40.593 --> 12:42.762
If you were to ever pick up
another weapon,

12:43.804 --> 12:45.306
you'd become a killer again.

12:45.389 --> 12:47.308
[ominous music playing]

12:47.391 --> 12:49.059
And who gave you the right to judge?

12:49.143 --> 12:50.936
We have a few things in common.

12:51.687 --> 12:53.689
We both suffered as children.

12:54.857 --> 12:56.650
We're both obsessed with revenge.

12:57.902 --> 13:00.237
And our lives are defined by guns.

13:00.738 --> 13:04.408
You can't justify your actions
with some sort of grade-school philosophy.

13:06.368 --> 13:09.246
You're nothing but a pimp
peddling guns for money.

13:11.415 --> 13:12.792
All you do is incite fear.

13:12.875 --> 13:14.919
- [music fades]
- [scoffs]

13:15.461 --> 13:16.337
[tuts]

13:18.005 --> 13:20.966
To be honest,
none of that matters to me anymore,

13:21.050 --> 13:23.093
whether or not I sell another gun.

13:23.177 --> 13:24.053
[tense music playing]

13:24.136 --> 13:26.263
Now I'm just curious to see

13:26.847 --> 13:29.099
what'll happen to the little hero in you,

13:29.642 --> 13:33.103
who truly thinks
that… guns aren't the true answer.

13:35.439 --> 13:36.982
[scoffs]

13:37.066 --> 13:42.112
The crazy thing about it, though,
was that it was way easier than I thought.

13:44.615 --> 13:47.493
A gun was the only option they had left.

13:48.202 --> 13:50.871
All that pent-up resentment
and frustration

13:50.955 --> 13:52.456
had to have an outlet.

13:59.213 --> 14:00.840
[Do] Nah, I don't need anything. Thanks.

14:02.716 --> 14:05.219
Excuse me. Something's buzzing on you.

14:06.470 --> 14:08.639
That was the case
with your beloved sergeant,

14:08.722 --> 14:10.099
who was like a father to you.

14:10.182 --> 14:12.226
[tense music continues]

14:14.478 --> 14:15.980
And with Kyeong-suk.

14:22.278 --> 14:23.654
In the end, it was a gun…

14:24.572 --> 14:25.823
I wanna thank you.

14:26.407 --> 14:27.616
…that saved them.

14:28.534 --> 14:30.202
[music swells]

14:30.286 --> 14:32.079
[music fades]

14:37.918 --> 14:41.005
In a world
where the strong devour the weak…

14:43.841 --> 14:46.385
even your bleeding heart
couldn't protect them.

14:47.011 --> 14:51.181
A weapon that allows them to express
how they truly feel is the answer.

14:52.224 --> 14:56.061
That's why putting more guns
into the world will lead to a new utopia.

14:57.479 --> 15:00.649
When everyone has a gun,
then we'll all be like you.

15:01.150 --> 15:02.735
- You're wrong.
- [ominous music playing]

15:02.818 --> 15:04.570
No such utopia exists.

15:06.739 --> 15:09.033
What you're describing
is pure destruction.

15:11.368 --> 15:12.870
People killing and being killed.

15:14.663 --> 15:15.873
[chuckles softly]

15:16.457 --> 15:17.583
That's disappointing.

15:23.297 --> 15:24.506
Of all people…

15:27.801 --> 15:29.470
I thought you would understand the most.

15:31.680 --> 15:32.681
Well,

15:33.557 --> 15:34.767
let's see, shall we?

15:35.935 --> 15:36.936
Who of us is right?

15:37.978 --> 15:39.980
[menacing musical sting]

15:40.064 --> 15:42.066
[tense music playing]

15:44.777 --> 15:47.029
- [protesters screaming]
- [horn blares]

15:47.112 --> 15:48.781
[panicked chatter, screaming]

15:58.374 --> 16:00.376
[protesters murmuring]

16:05.839 --> 16:06.799
What are you doing?

16:09.218 --> 16:11.220
[tense music continues]

16:12.388 --> 16:14.974
I'll show you
the world I would like to live in.

16:16.183 --> 16:17.393
Make yourself at home.

16:17.893 --> 16:19.895
[foreboding music playing]

16:24.858 --> 16:26.860
[indistinct chatter]

16:28.362 --> 16:29.655
[elevator door opens]

16:34.326 --> 16:35.285
[gun clicks]

16:46.505 --> 16:48.132
[music fades]

16:55.222 --> 16:57.224
[indistinct chatter]

16:59.393 --> 17:00.436
[man speaking indistinctly]

17:03.063 --> 17:05.482
- [speaker feedback]
- [protesters scream]

17:07.359 --> 17:09.236
[woman] What kind of maniac does that?!

17:09.737 --> 17:13.073
Those are guns you're looking at.
So what are you waiting for?

17:13.157 --> 17:15.284
- [tense music playing]
- Hurry up and take 'em.

17:16.493 --> 17:17.911
It's filled with guns!

17:17.995 --> 17:19.121
[protesters clamoring]

17:24.710 --> 17:26.462
There are guns in here! Come on!

17:27.671 --> 17:29.048
[clamoring continues]

17:29.131 --> 17:30.591
[tense music continues]

17:31.341 --> 17:32.217
Take this!

17:32.926 --> 17:34.053
[men grunting]

17:35.888 --> 17:37.139
- [gunshot]
- [groans]

17:37.222 --> 17:38.348
[automatic gunfire]

17:38.432 --> 17:40.392
[men groaning]

17:40.476 --> 17:42.269
[siren wails]

17:42.352 --> 17:44.938
[officers] Guns are being distributed
from the truck.

17:45.022 --> 17:46.523
Citizens are swarming to it.

17:55.449 --> 17:57.201
[rapid gunfire]

17:58.786 --> 18:00.162
[gunfire stops]

18:03.957 --> 18:04.792
[man screams]

18:07.753 --> 18:09.671
[clamoring continues]

18:16.845 --> 18:19.098
[men yelling]

18:19.181 --> 18:21.100
[protesters screaming]

18:22.684 --> 18:25.104
- Ask Special Ops to send backup.
- Yes, sir.

18:28.023 --> 18:29.441
[dramatic music playing]

18:53.257 --> 18:54.258
[man on TV] Breaking news.

18:54.341 --> 18:58.512
There was a massive distribution
of firearms at today's pro-gun rally.

18:59.304 --> 19:00.931
The citizens became entangled,

19:01.014 --> 19:03.851
quickly descending the rally into chaos.

19:04.810 --> 19:06.353
Police have cordoned off the area

19:06.436 --> 19:09.356
with concerns of a large-scale shootout
taking place.

19:09.439 --> 19:13.360
They've announced they're doing their best
to confiscate all the guns distributed.

19:13.986 --> 19:17.197
We will continue to provide updates
as more information becomes available.

19:17.698 --> 19:19.700
[music fades]

19:24.872 --> 19:26.081
[gun clicks]

19:50.981 --> 19:53.108
[protesters clamoring]

19:53.692 --> 19:55.360
[whistle blowing]

19:58.155 --> 19:59.448
[distant object clatters]

20:05.162 --> 20:08.248
You'd better not stop rolling that camera.
Get it all.

20:08.332 --> 20:10.417
- Okay.
- ["This Is War" playing]

20:10.500 --> 20:13.212
♪ "Welcome to the city" ♪

20:13.295 --> 20:17.216
♪ Said a young man
Sitting next to me ♪

20:17.299 --> 20:19.009
♪ "Heard you're new in town" ♪

20:19.092 --> 20:20.594
♪ "Before you get around…" ♪

20:20.677 --> 20:22.054
Give it to me, God damn it!

20:22.137 --> 20:24.139
♪ "Here's a little tip from me…" ♪

20:25.224 --> 20:27.768
What are we supposed to do
when you take away our freedom?!

20:27.851 --> 20:30.646
- We can't take it anymore! You hear me?
- Just put the gun down.

20:30.729 --> 20:34.024
We're not doing anything wrong!
We just wanna protect each other.

20:34.107 --> 20:36.360
- And you won't say we can't!
- [woman 2] Let's run!

20:36.443 --> 20:37.861
- No. No.
- [woman 1] Leave us alone!

20:37.945 --> 20:40.864
You can't even walk down the street
anymore without getting murdered!

20:40.948 --> 20:42.574
Disrespect! I need this to protect--

20:42.658 --> 20:45.535
- Hey! Grab the gun!
- Get off!

20:45.619 --> 20:49.414
♪ Where the little man
Pays a bigger price ♪

20:49.498 --> 20:52.626
♪ Take another hit
Just get it over with… ♪

20:52.709 --> 20:55.420
FIREARMS DISTRIBUTED AT RALLY
SCENE IN PANIC

20:57.047 --> 21:00.384
♪ Can't stay down no more
We gotta make it known ♪

21:00.467 --> 21:04.012
♪ So get back up
You're not alone ♪

21:04.096 --> 21:07.683
♪ And then hit 'em back
Leave 'em gripping to the floor ♪

21:07.766 --> 21:10.602
♪ You never had a choice
They're knocking at your door… ♪

21:10.686 --> 21:12.562
FIREARMS DISTRIBUTED AT RALLY
SCENE IN PANIC

21:12.646 --> 21:16.233
♪ It's time
And this is war… ♪

21:16.316 --> 21:20.988
UNEXPECTED FIREARM DISTRIBUTION
SPARKS CHAOS AT RALLY

21:21.071 --> 21:27.995
♪ It's time
And this is war ♪

21:34.710 --> 21:38.255
♪ Whoa-oh, whoa-oh-oh, oh-oh, oh ♪

21:38.338 --> 21:44.261
♪ Oh, oh-oh, oh-oh
Oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh-oh ♪

21:50.851 --> 21:53.478
♪ Welcome to the untold ♪

21:53.979 --> 21:57.357
♪ Take a deep breath
Take the higher road… ♪

21:57.441 --> 21:59.192
[Moon Baek] See what I mean, Lee Do?

22:00.610 --> 22:04.990
If, as you say, a world where everyone has
a gun is pure destruction…

22:05.073 --> 22:06.033
[inaudible]

22:06.616 --> 22:09.911
…then why do so many people
want them in their hands?

22:12.080 --> 22:13.999
Isn't it more of a paradise

22:15.083 --> 22:17.544
to give people what they truly desire?

22:19.463 --> 22:21.423
♪ The day has come, my friend ♪

22:21.506 --> 22:26.428
♪ 'Cause this is war ♪

22:28.889 --> 22:30.057
♪ It's time ♪

22:30.140 --> 22:36.855
♪ And this is war ♪

22:40.692 --> 22:42.694
[music fades]

22:43.195 --> 22:44.696
[pin rattles]

22:45.614 --> 22:47.616
- [gas hissing]
- [somber music playing]

22:50.535 --> 22:53.622
[whistle blowing]

22:53.705 --> 22:55.707
- [whooshing]
- [clamoring continues]

23:13.767 --> 23:15.769
[somber music continues]

23:19.815 --> 23:21.191
[Moon Baek] It's this world

23:22.526 --> 23:24.319
that makes people violent.

23:24.403 --> 23:26.405
[footsteps echoing]

23:27.197 --> 23:29.116
All I did was hand them a gun.

23:29.658 --> 23:31.660
I didn't force them to pull the trigger.

23:33.203 --> 23:35.747
The decision has
always been theirs to make.

23:36.248 --> 23:38.250
I didn't pull the trigger for them.

23:38.333 --> 23:40.335
[footsteps echoing]

23:42.546 --> 23:44.548
[clamoring continues]

23:44.631 --> 23:46.633
[gas hissing]

23:51.221 --> 23:53.140
- [tense music playing]
- [exhales sharply]

23:53.223 --> 23:54.307
[Moon Baek] Lee Do.

23:58.103 --> 24:00.647
If a gunshot went off here, right now,

24:01.356 --> 24:03.692
what do you think
would happen to these people?

24:04.443 --> 24:06.194
So was this your plan all along?

24:06.695 --> 24:08.447
[whistle blowing]

24:09.698 --> 24:10.657
[Moon Baek] Not really.

24:12.576 --> 24:13.869
What I really want

24:14.411 --> 24:16.413
is the sound of a single gunshot.

24:17.706 --> 24:19.708
[tense music continues]

24:26.298 --> 24:27.382
One shot

24:27.966 --> 24:29.926
that'll turn this whole place

24:31.678 --> 24:33.388
into a war zone.

24:41.271 --> 24:45.233
Wouldn't pulling the trigger on any gun,
in the pursuit of revenge,

24:46.818 --> 24:48.778
just take control away from the people?

24:49.404 --> 24:51.364
They'd all be afraid
that if they don't have a gun,

24:51.448 --> 24:54.993
they might die.
So everyone would be desperate to get one.

24:56.745 --> 25:00.373
And that kind of society
would kill itself off.

25:01.625 --> 25:03.627
[tense music continues]

25:05.754 --> 25:07.380
[whooshing]

25:07.464 --> 25:09.466
[clamoring continues]

25:18.266 --> 25:19.267
[gunshot]

25:23.647 --> 25:26.066
- [music intensifies]
- [gasps]

25:35.784 --> 25:38.161
- [music fades]
- [Moon Baek breathing heavily]

25:51.758 --> 25:53.760
[protesters screaming, clamoring]

25:54.511 --> 25:56.513
[rapid gunfire]

26:01.726 --> 26:03.103
[stirring music playing]

26:04.688 --> 26:07.107
- [gunfire continues]
- [screaming continues]

26:11.945 --> 26:14.239
[Moon Baek breathing shakily]

26:24.833 --> 26:25.917
- [gunshot]
- [groans]

26:26.001 --> 26:27.294
[grunts]

26:28.086 --> 26:28.962
[gunshot]

26:29.045 --> 26:31.047
[protesters screaming]

26:31.881 --> 26:33.883
[rapid gunfire]

26:34.759 --> 26:36.761
[child sobbing]

26:41.808 --> 26:43.810
[sobbing continues]

26:51.234 --> 26:53.236
[stirring music continues]

26:57.157 --> 26:59.159
[Do panting]

27:01.661 --> 27:03.663
[child sobbing continues]

27:09.336 --> 27:11.338
[sobbing continues]

27:13.632 --> 27:16.092
[boy] Someone help me!

27:23.058 --> 27:24.726
- Mama…
- [whooshing]

27:25.518 --> 27:27.520
[boy breathing shakily]

27:32.567 --> 27:33.693
You'll be okay.

27:36.112 --> 27:37.447
I've got you.

27:42.327 --> 27:44.329
[stirring music continues]

28:08.478 --> 28:10.480
[stirring music continues]

28:23.785 --> 28:25.787
[music fades]

28:29.332 --> 28:31.334
[somber music playing]

28:31.418 --> 28:34.337
GUN DISTRIBUTION SPARKS
ESCALATING VIOLENCE AT RALLY

28:40.301 --> 28:43.471
[male reporter 1] Tragedy struck today
in the heart of the city.

28:43.555 --> 28:46.558
So far,
the mass shooting at Gyeongin Stadium

28:47.058 --> 28:50.645
has reportedly resulted
in more than 70 casualties.

28:51.604 --> 28:53.148
The death toll is sure to increase…

28:53.231 --> 28:54.649
POLICE DISCUSSING EMERGENCY RESPONSE

28:54.733 --> 28:58.027
…seeing as many civilians
have been critically injured.

29:00.363 --> 29:03.116
[male reporter 2] In the midst
of the shooting at Gyeongin Stadium,

29:03.199 --> 29:05.076
a heartwarming image of a citizen

29:05.160 --> 29:07.078
who saved the life of a child.

29:08.997 --> 29:11.833
The citizen protected the child
amidst all the gunfire,

29:11.916 --> 29:13.960
putting his own life in danger.

29:14.502 --> 29:16.755
It is said
he proceeded to comfort the child…

29:18.840 --> 29:20.842
[somber music continues]

29:38.193 --> 29:39.360
[camera shutter clicks]

29:54.626 --> 30:01.633
WE WILL PRAY FOR THE VICTIMS

30:06.638 --> 30:08.640
[somber music continues]

30:09.641 --> 30:16.648
WE WILL REMEMBER THE INNOCENT LIVES LOST
AND WORK TO CREATE A SAFER WORLD

30:16.731 --> 30:20.735
MAY THE VICTIMS REST IN PEACE

30:20.819 --> 30:22.237
[music fades]

30:26.783 --> 30:27.659
ANTI-GUN PETITION

30:27.742 --> 30:30.203
[woman 1] We're collecting signatures
for an anti-gun petition.

30:30.286 --> 30:32.038
- [woman 2] Yes.
- [woman 3] Of course you can.

30:32.121 --> 30:33.623
You just have to sign right there.

30:33.706 --> 30:35.250
ILLEGAL FIREARM DROP-OFF POINT

30:36.459 --> 30:37.877
Thank you for volunteering.

30:38.670 --> 30:39.504
Fine.

30:39.587 --> 30:40.588
Thank you so much.

30:43.049 --> 30:44.300
[Jeong-u sighs]

30:47.720 --> 30:50.306
- You're turning over a handgun, right?
- Yes.

30:50.974 --> 30:52.225
I have no use for it.

30:56.312 --> 30:57.730
You made the right choice.

31:01.943 --> 31:03.444
Sign here, if you please.

31:07.574 --> 31:09.784
PARK SO-HYEON, FEMALE

31:12.370 --> 31:13.830
Very good. Thank you.

31:21.629 --> 31:23.590
[Dae-hyeon] Whoa-ho-ho-ho, man!

31:23.673 --> 31:26.718
The view from this room is amazing.

31:26.801 --> 31:28.052
Yeah, you were right.

31:28.803 --> 31:30.763
Yeah, I could use this room. Yeah.

31:32.599 --> 31:33.433
What?

31:33.516 --> 31:37.103
Why would you censor my article to protect
the victims? Who cares about them?!

31:37.812 --> 31:39.564
I'm telling you right now

31:40.356 --> 31:43.026
if you touch one word without permission,

31:43.109 --> 31:45.820
I'm moving to a different network.
Is that clear?

31:50.617 --> 31:52.869
- [Dae-hyeon sighs]
- [unsettling music playing]

31:53.870 --> 31:55.622
Holy shit! What the hell?!

31:55.705 --> 31:57.540
Do you have any idea

31:58.249 --> 32:00.919
what your article did
to the lives of the innocent?

32:01.753 --> 32:04.464
After I begged
and pleaded to have it taken down?

32:04.547 --> 32:05.673
[Dae-hyeon] Wait, wait. Wait.

32:05.757 --> 32:07.675
I'm the reporter. I'll take it down--

32:07.759 --> 32:09.010
[groans]

32:09.093 --> 32:10.219
[body thuds]

32:10.303 --> 32:12.305
[unsettling music continues]

32:36.913 --> 32:40.333
Given his significant blood loss
and history of cancer,

32:41.000 --> 32:43.378
it'll be difficult for him
to make a recovery.

32:48.007 --> 32:50.009
[unsettling music continues]

32:57.266 --> 32:59.268
[monitor beeping steadily]

33:02.105 --> 33:03.940
[Jake] If you wanna call yourself
a businessman,

33:04.023 --> 33:07.986
you'd better be making five dollars
for every one you spend, at least.

33:09.529 --> 33:10.655
We have an opening.

33:11.864 --> 33:13.408
Proceed as planned.

33:13.491 --> 33:15.493
[unsettling music continues]

33:21.040 --> 33:22.542
[monitor beeping steadily]

33:39.100 --> 33:41.102
[music fades]

33:57.702 --> 33:59.704
[poignant music playing]

34:01.748 --> 34:02.749
I'm good.

34:05.334 --> 34:06.294
Thank you.

34:07.003 --> 34:07.879
[exhales sharply]

34:19.932 --> 34:21.934
[poignant music continues]

34:26.481 --> 34:28.483
[children chatter]

34:55.343 --> 34:57.345
[poignant music continues]

35:07.271 --> 35:09.273
[inaudible]

35:21.410 --> 35:23.412
[music fades]

35:38.511 --> 35:40.513
[funky rock music playing]

38:27.763 --> 38:29.557
[music fades]

38:29.640 --> 38:31.642
[gentle guitar music playing]

39:34.580 --> 39:36.582
[music fades]
